                <pb facs="0336" n="254" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg254"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.001G29/53.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">His Majesty King George V to the
                    President.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-06-22"><hi rendition="#italic">June 22,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I heartily thank you and the people of the United States for the very kind
                    congratulations which you offer me on this great and <pb facs="0337" n="255"
                        xml:id="pg255"/> solemn day, and for the good wishes which you express for
                    the prosperity of the British dominions and for the welfare of myself and my
                    family. I heartily reciprocate your wishes that the friendly relations between
                    the United States and my country may ever continue.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">George, R. I.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
